# Evolusea Coding Standards

## Validation
- Request validation: `class-validator` decorators on DTOs
- Global `ValidationPipe` with `transform: true` and `whitelist: true`
- Domain validation: `BusinessRule` pattern with `checkRule()` / `checkAsyncRule()`

## Testing Requirements
- Unit tests use `.spec.ts` suffix, co-located with source
- E2E tests in `test/` directory using Testcontainers (real PostgreSQL)
- Smoke tests for deployed API health checks
- Use `AiFakeFacade` for testing AI-dependent features
- Use `TestAppFactory` for E2E test bootstrapping

## Database
- Migrations only — never `synchronize: true`
- Auto-generate: `yarn run migration:autogenerate src/migrations/<Name>`
- SnakeNamingStrategy for all table/column names
- UUID primary keys, TIMESTAMPTZ for all timestamps

## Module Registration
- New domain modules must be imported in `src/http-app/http-app.module.ts`
- New controllers go in `src/http-app/controllers/`
- Facades are provided at the module level with `{ provide: AbstractFacade, useClass: RealFacade }`

## Error Handling
- Domain errors: throw specific error types (e.g., `DomainRuleViolationError`, `EntityNotFoundError`)
- HTTP layer: `ExceptionFilter` maps domain errors to HTTP responses
- Never catch and swallow errors silently

## Scheduled Tasks
- Use `@Cron()` decorator from `@nestjs/schedule`
- All times in UTC (server timezone)
- Always use distributed locking for tasks that modify data
- Bangkok = UTC+7 (so midnight Bangkok = 17:00 UTC)
